{"title":"2020 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 3c","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Modular_Arithmetic)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Modular Arithmetic)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2020 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a <i>Dlin sequence</i>, the first term is a positive integer and each term after the first is calculated by adding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to the previous term in the sequence, then doubling the result. For example, the first seven terms of the Dlin sequence with first term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are:\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/b/0ab734f0d1d149f394bac30bed297bd11a88a924.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4, 10, 22, 46, 94, 190, 382$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"187\" height=\"17\" /></center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Which possible first terms from 10 to 19 inclusive produce a Dlin sequence in which all terms after the first have the same ones (units) digit?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can split by cases based on the first term and use only the units digit. This can be done through a table as well.\n</p><p>If the first term of a Dlin sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, the units digit of the first term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, the units digit of the next term would be the same as the units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/a/ffad5c86b21d7f5e06fadfc3a11f39d37e17473c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(0 + 1) = 2 \\times 1 = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"163\" height=\"20\" />, which has a units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The units digit of the next term after this would be the same as the units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/e/8bef000650234be779b9d9b27767cabd79de5d41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(2 + 1) = 2 \\times 3 = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"163\" height=\"20\" />, which has a units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. However, we notice these units digits are not the same, so the first term cannot be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>If the first term of a Dlin sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, the units digit of the first term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, the units digit of the next term would be the same as the units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/e/13e2dc4c60d00a3ab9f3538ff23520a7b66c884b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(1 + 1) = 2 \\times 2 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"163\" height=\"20\" />, which has a units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The units digit of the next term after this would be the same as the units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/d/3ed14014de5a53579942b8fda81bd42ee72eaf9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(4 + 1) = 2 \\times 5 = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"173\" height=\"20\" />, which has a units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. However, we notice these units digits are not the same, so the first term cannot be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>If the first term of a Dlin sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, the units digit of the first term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, the units digit of the next term would be the same as the units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/e/8bef000650234be779b9d9b27767cabd79de5d41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(2 + 1) = 2 \\times 3 = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"163\" height=\"20\" />, which has a units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The units digit of the next term after this would be the same as the units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/3/c5341f8e7f21d018319640528933d8127b0795c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(6 + 1) = 2 \\times 7 = 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"173\" height=\"20\" />, which has a units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. However, we notice these units digits are not the same, so the first term cannot be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>If the first term of a Dlin sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, the units digit of the first term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, the units digit of the next term would be the same as the units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/c/e6c416d40046517d63cbfea48af98a0897989d0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(3 + 1) = 2 \\times 4 = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"163\" height=\"20\" />, which has a units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The units digit of the next term after this would be the same as the units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/b/f1b898c170683fc6a27327d052c9799a8fd4bc02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(8 + 1) = 2 \\times 9 = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"173\" height=\"20\" />, which has a units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. These units digits are the same and we realize this pattern would just repeat, so the first term of a Dlin sequence can be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>If the first term of a Dlin sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, the units digit of the first term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, the units digit of the next term would be the same as the units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/d/3ed14014de5a53579942b8fda81bd42ee72eaf9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(4 + 1) = 2 \\times 5 = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"173\" height=\"20\" />, which has a units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The second term would then have a units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, like when the first term was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. However, we notice these units digits are not the same, so the first term cannot be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>If the first term of a Dlin sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, the units digit of the first term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, the units digit of the next term would be the same as the units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/e/5aea1f263be977f764708dba471ff41d1b75bb69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(5 + 1) = 2 \\times 6 = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"173\" height=\"20\" />, which has a units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The units digit of the next term after this would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, like with the first term being <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. However, we notice these units digits are not the same, so the first term cannot be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>If the first term of a Dlin sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, the units digit of the first term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, the units digit of the next term would be the same as the units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/3/c5341f8e7f21d018319640528933d8127b0795c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(6 + 1) = 2 \\times 7 = 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"173\" height=\"20\" />, which has a units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The units digit of the next term after this would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, like with the first term being <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. However, we notice these units digits are not the same, so the first term cannot be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>If the first term of a Dlin sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, the units digit of the first term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, the units digit of the next term would be the same as the units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/7/bb71e8841117cf25a31f4aea688aa509f2672119.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(7 + 1) = 2 \\times 8 = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"173\" height=\"20\" />, which has a units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The units digit of the next term after this would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, like with the first term being <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. However, we notice these units digits are not the same, so the first term cannot be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>If the first term of a Dlin sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, the units digit of the first term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. We noticed previously that when the units digit is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the next units digit would have to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> as well, so the first term can be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>If the first term of a Dlin sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efbfe273946ff9f971c5eab331ca39caa6fdf7f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, the units digit of the first term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, the units digit of the next term would be the same as the units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/7/e7791cd1b2a12b9301a3f2506f1892bcc43b3e43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(9 + 1) = 2 \\times 10 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"173\" height=\"20\" />, which has a units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The units digit of the next term after this would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, like with the first term being <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. However, we notice these units digits are not the same, so the first term cannot be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efbfe273946ff9f971c5eab331ca39caa6fdf7f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, the first term of a Dlin sequence can be either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/e/25e40bc2b9bcef49b195e9be1e88febb6eff5fd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"23\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/7/707b150be2f7a929f705d880caa88481445f9a87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{18}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Modular_Arithmetic.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Modular_Arithmetic)\">Solution 2 (Modular Arithmetic)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Modular Arithmetic)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/2/bd28b278a07bda0ea4d08737743613980c6aa6a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> be the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /><sup>th</sup> term of the sequence. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/7/577f233ff970bde00137808bfa15c1e96df56f9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> would then be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/2/dd2660e6e9d0cb2c9f2a57603a68aa6a5e0543c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(a_{2} + 1) = 2a_{2} + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"155\" height=\"20\" />. This must have the same units digit as the second term, so we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/1/591c2918f48515dc971910220fb34446c8289593.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2} \\equiv 2a_{2} + 2 \\pmod{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"182\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/3/883e54d0f6f6b49ccfdb205f044201edc9a86689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2} \\equiv -2 \\pmod {10} \\equiv 8 \\pmod {10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"262\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>We can then notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/9/199bbd4e91050883d9a86770d240cf2d3a85539d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> would have a units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/9/199bbd4e91050883d9a86770d240cf2d3a85539d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> is also equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/5/0f5b2ae7df08cc731ebb7278318a280f3de82070.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a_{1} + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"17\" />, so we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/5/8f5950862ac7f0954a5827e1549b331cbb4d126f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a_{1} + 2 \\equiv 8 \\pmod {10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"174\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/f/13f57d3d7a044ea200ff21db6396b4c75104794a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a_{1} \\equiv 6 \\pmod {10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"143\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>We can realize that this would occur when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/a/1da7198d9a79e0a6dc32e60162044ee0f726e4e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> has a units digit of either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/a/1da7198d9a79e0a6dc32e60162044ee0f726e4e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> is between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efbfe273946ff9f971c5eab331ca39caa6fdf7f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/a/1da7198d9a79e0a6dc32e60162044ee0f726e4e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> would either be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/e/25e40bc2b9bcef49b195e9be1e88febb6eff5fd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"23\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/7/707b150be2f7a929f705d880caa88481445f9a87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{18}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017035232\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.029 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.044 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 435/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 452/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 16694/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    8.673      1 2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3\n100.00%    8.673      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36616:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017035232 and revision id 285650. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}